{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>This time [is] different</b><br>My conception [and] my birth, like [the example of] the blessings of my parents." "<b>This time [is] different</b><br>And a short time — less than a year — had passed when the Shekhinah ascanced within me [and] descended in the Tabernacle, and they desired to enter the land and said, 'Here we are.'"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "Reading עבר as 'had passed'; the clause structure is compressed and the subject of ורצו/ואמרו is left unstated by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:10.134071397Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}